 in 2109. After working with record keepers to cross-check registers, he became register clerk of the Guro–Geumcheon axis mobilization register. In 2126 he negotiates a subcontract with Pham Van Duc and inspects Lin Xiaomei''s passage, and he is wary of the deserter platoon using the register as a basis for a private-soldier organization. Keeping the keys and the register separate is a choice made to protect the work entrusted to him. Choe Ilseok was born in Guro in 2087. After serving as an enlisted soldier in the contemporary Mobilization Remnant and returning upon completing his term in 2109, he cross-checked the shift register with his father Choe Taeyun. As register clerk of the Guro–Geumcheon axis mobilization register, he verifies actual service and return records, and is wary of the register being used as a basis for a private-soldier organization. His great-grandfather Choe Gyeongseop, born in 1997, carried out the reserve-force company''s register around 2026 and distinguished the people who could be contacted from those who had evacuated. His son Choe Munjae separated the old evacuation list from the current duty roster, and his grandson Choe Taeyun cross-checked the shift register. After completing his service in 2109, Choe Ilseok verified actual service and return records together with his father.","sourceRefs":[{"path":"lore/name-pools/diaspora-family-lineages.json","anchor":"guro-choi-family/K1016"}]},{"year":2110,"summary":"Choe Ilseok, born in Guro, served as an enlisted soldier in the contemporary Mobilization Remnant and returned upon completing his term in 2109. After working with record keepers to cross-check registers, he became register clerk of the Guro–Geumcheon axis mobilization register. In 2126 he negotiates a subcontract with Pham Van Duc and inspects Lin Xiaomei''s passage, and he is wary of the deserter platoon using the register as a basis for a private-soldier organization. Keeping the keys and the register separate is a choice made 